# React 19 Frontend Rules

## Component Guidelines
- Use functional components with React 19 features
- Prefer `useState`, `useReducer`, and `useRef` for state management
- Use React 19's `use` hook for async data loading when applicable
- Keep components small and composable
- One component per file, named in PascalCase

## File Organization
- Components: `/src/components/` - Reusable UI components
- Admin components: `/src/components/admin/` - Admin-specific components
- Services: `/src/services/` - API calls and business logic
- Hooks: `/src/hooks/` - Custom React hooks
- Utils: `/src/utils/` - Utility functions

## Styling
- Use TailwindCSS classes for styling
- Dark mode support via `dark:` prefix
- Custom animations defined in [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js)
- Prefer TailwindCSS over CSS modules

## Key Components
- [src/components/MemberDashboard.jsx](mdc:src/components/MemberDashboard.jsx) - Main member interface
- [src/components/admin/AdminDashboard.jsx](mdc:src/components/admin/AdminDashboard.jsx) - Admin interface
- [src/components/Rounds.jsx](mdc:src/components/Rounds.jsx) - Competition rounds
- [src/components/News.jsx](mdc:src/components/News.jsx) - News display
- [src/components/CityTips.jsx](mdc:src/components/CityTips.jsx) - Location recommendations

## Performance
- Use lazy loading with `React.lazy()` and `Suspense`
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Optimize images with [src/components/LazyImage.jsx](mdc:src/components/LazyImage.jsx)
- Use [src/components/SkeletonLoader.jsx](mdc:src/components/SkeletonLoader.jsx) for loading states